<!--
    Declared Swift prototypes, the four-register return, the indirect
    result register and the async context (`option swiftcall on|off`).

    Issue: a Swift image that kept its symbols spells every method's
    signature in its mangled name, and Swift returns up to four words in
    registers where C passes a struct of 17 bytes through the indirect
    result register, takes that register as rax (not rdi) on x86-64, and
    hands an `async` function its task context in r14; under the C model a
    three-word return is a `rethidden` pointer in the first argument
    register, the real first argument slides over, and the context is an
    unnamed register.

    Stage / sub-stage: P1 external-refinement (`kuna_swiftcall.rs`, the
    declared prototypes) and P4 prototype models (`kuna_swiftcall::derive_model`).

    P0 assertion: `option swiftcall on|off` (default on).

    Both passes load the real fixture `swift_sigs_syms_elf` (x86-64 ELF,
    swiftc 6.3, symbols kept) with `swiftmetadata on`. Pass 1 (`option
    swiftcall off`): `Box.triple(_:)` is recovered as `undefined16 (long a0)`,
    without its `self` or its struct. Pass 2
    (the default): it returns `sigfix.Triple` in `rcx:rdx:rax` with its
    declared `(long a0, sigfix.Box *self)`, `Box.wide(_:)` takes its
    `sigfix.Wide *rethidden` in rax ahead of `a0`, `Box.slow(_:)` takes
    `swift.AsyncContext *async_context` with the context's layout, `sum3`
    takes a three-word struct by value and `sum5` a five-word one by
    address, `swap2` a tuple in and out, `hashed<A: Hashable>` the metadata
    and witness table after its arguments, `Triple.sum()` its `self` by value
    and `Triple.bump(_:)` by address, and an accessor returns a
    `swift.MetadataResponse`.
-->
